  "question": {
    "html": "<p>An atom has the energy levels shown in the table below. The atom is initially in its ground state (<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n = 1\"></span>).</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Energy level</th><th>Energy / eV</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n = 1\"></span> (ground state)</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"-12.0\"></span></td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n = 2\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"-7.0\"></span></td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n = 3\"></span></td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"-2.0\"></span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>An electron with a kinetic energy of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"9.0\"></span> eV collides with the atom. Which of the following is a possible kinetic energy of the electron after it has collided with the atom and caused an atomic excitation?</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th></th><th>Kinetic energy / eV</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr data-label=\"A\"><td>A.</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.0\"></span></td></tr><tr data-label=\"B\"><td>B.</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4.0\"></span></td></tr><tr data-label=\"C\"><td>C.</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5.0\"></span></td></tr><tr data-label=\"D\"><td>D.</td><td><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"7.0\"></span></td></tr></tbody></table>"
  },
